SOAPBOX: Elecraft K3S, 500w, C19XR @ 55', N1MM+, MMTTY & 2-Tone
SOAPBOX: Happy wife, happy life...that was the theme of this contest...no Saturday
SOAPBOX: operating as I had committed to a project for the XYL... But I tried
SOAPBOX: my best to make up for it with some operating Saturday evening & all day
SOAPBOX: Sunday...It seemed at times like the whole world was on 15m...I was copying
SOAPBOX: stations all the way up to 21.170... Wow!!... great to see the turnout in a big
SOAPBOX: RTTY test...
SOAPBOX: I worked 46 states on one band in just 16 hours... missing just the in close states. (VT,CT,DE & WV)
SOAPBOX: I logged into a local DX-spotting network, but did not use it for one qso...
SOAPBOX: just hard to shake old habit of always running unassisted, but can't in good faith claim Classic... too bad,as it would be near the top in NA scores.
SOAPBOX: Had fun, thank you to all who got on and made it into log
SOAPBOX: 73, Neil AE1P
